[4356.954714, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[57;2H\u001b(B\u001b[0;7mL\u001b(B\u001b[m Refresh         \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m^W\u001b(B\u001b[m Where Is        \u001b(B\u001b[0;7mM-Q\u001b(B\u001b[m Previous       \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m^P\u001b(B\u001b[m Prev Line       \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m^Y\u001b(B\u001b[m Prev Page       \u001b(B\u001b[0;7mM-\\\u001b(B\u001b[m First Line\u001b[58;4HClose\u001b[58;17H   \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m^Q\u001b(B\u001b[m Where Was       \u001b(B\u001b[0;7mM-W\u001b(B\u001b[m Next           \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m^N\u001b(B\u001b[m Next Line       \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m^V\u001b(B\u001b[m Next Page       \u001b(B\u001b[0;7mM-/\u001b(B\u001b[m Last Line\r\u001b[56d\u001b[1;3H\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m            \u001b[1;50HMain nano help text\u001b[1;108H        \u001b(B\u001b[m\r\u001b[2d\u001b[39;49m\u001b(B\u001b[m The nano editor is designed to emulate the functionality and ease-of-use\r\u001b[3d of the UW Pico text editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.\r\u001b[4d The top line shows the program version, the current filename being\r\u001b[5d edited, and whether or not the file has been modified.  Next is the main\r\u001b[6d editor window showing the file being edited.  The status line is the\r\u001b[7d third line from the bottom and shows important messages.  The bottom two\r\u001b[8d lines show the most commonly used shortcuts in the editor.\r\u001b[10d Sh"]
[4356.955234, "o", "ortcuts are written as follows: Control-key sequences are notated with\r\u001b[11d a \u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[31m'^'\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or pressing the Esc\r\u001b[12d key twice.  Meta-key sequences are notated with \u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[31m'M-'\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m and can be entered\r\u001b[13d using either the Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.\r\u001b[14d Also, pressing Esc twice and then typing a three-digit decimal number\r\u001b[15d from 000 to 255 will enter the character with the corresponding value.\r\u001b[16d The following keystrokes are available in the main editor window.\r\u001b[17d Alternative keys are shown in parentheses:\r\u001b[19d\u001b[36m^G\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mF1\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GDisplay this help text\r\u001b[20d\u001b[36m^X\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mF2\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GClose the current buffer / Exit from nano\r\u001b[21d\u001b[36m^O\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mF3\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GWrite the current buffer (or the marked region) to disk\r\u001b[22d\u001b[36m^R\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mIns\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)     Insert another file into current buffer (or into new buffe"]
[4356.95551, "o", "r)\r\u001b[24d\u001b[36m^W\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mF6\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GSearch forward for a string or a regular expression\r\u001b[25d\u001b[36m^\\\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mM-R\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)     Replace a string or a regular expression\r\u001b[26d\u001b[36m^K\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mF9\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GCut current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer\r\u001b[27d\u001b[36m^U\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mF10\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)     Paste the contents of cutbuffer at current cursor position\r\u001b[29d\u001b[36m^J\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mF4\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GJustify the current paragraph\r\u001b[30d\u001b[36m^T\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mF12\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)     Invoke the spell checker, if available\r\u001b[32d\u001b[36m^C\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mF11\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)     Display the position of the cursor\r\u001b[33d\u001b[36m^_\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mM-G\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)     Go to line and column number\r\u001b[35d\u001b[36mM-U\u001b[35;18H\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[mUndo the last operation\r\u001b[36d\u001b[36mM-E\u001b[36;18H\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[mRedo the last undone operation\r\u001b[38d\u001b[36mM-A\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m    (\u001b[36m^6\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GMark text starting from the cursor position\r\u001b[39d\u001b[36mM-6\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m    ("]
[4356.955761, "o", "\u001b[36mM-^\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)     Copy current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer\r\u001b[41d\u001b[36mM-]\u001b[41;18H\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[mGo to the matching bracket\r\u001b[43d\u001b[36m^Q\u001b[43;18H\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[mSearch backward for a string or a regular expression\r\u001b[44d\u001b[36mM-Q\u001b[44;18H\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[mSearch next occurrence backward\r\u001b[45d\u001b[36mM-W\u001b[45;18H\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[mSearch next occurrence forward\r\u001b[47d\u001b[36m^B\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36m◀\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GGo back one character\r\u001b[48d\u001b[36m^F\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36m▶\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GGo forward one character\r\u001b[49d\u001b[36m^◀\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mM-Space\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m) Go back one word\r\u001b[50d\u001b[36m^▶\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36m^Space\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)  Go forward one word\r\u001b[51d\u001b[36m^A\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mHome\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)    Go to beginning of current line\r\u001b[52d\u001b[36m^E\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36mEnd\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)     Go to end of current line\r\u001b[54d\u001b[36m^P\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36m▲\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GGo to previous line\r\u001b[55d\u001b[36m^N\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m     (\u001b[36m▼\u001b[39m\u001b(B\u001b[m)\u001b[18GGo to next line\r\u001b[2d"]
